Below is one acceptable solution in C. In this solution the string is assumed to be stored in a mutable character array (that is, the caller is allowed to modify the input). The algorithm meets the requirements because

• It runs in O(n) time (first finding the end, then reversing the whole string, then “fixing” each multi‐byte sequence).
• It uses only constant extra space (just a few pointer variables and a temporary char for swapping).
