Below is an example solution written in Python using Flask. In this design we use an in‐memory dictionary to store leaks (in a real application you would use a database), and a simple decorator to simulate user authentication and role‐based access. Flask’s request parsing and error handlers are used to validate incoming requests and return proper JSON error responses. You can adapt and extend this example as needed.

