Below is one example of how you might implement the gRPC‐based calendar service in Python. In this example we use Protocol Buffers (the .proto file is included), a CalendarServicer class with a RecieveData method that validates incoming reminder data (including verifying the email format using a regular expression), and a serve() function that starts the gRPC server and continuously polls scheduled reminders to “send” emails. (In a production environment you might use an external messaging queue and a production‐grade email service.) Any email sending errors will be caught and reported via a dummy error handling service function.

For simplicity the code uses in‑memory storage for pending reminders and a background thread that “sleeps” until a reminder is due. You can later extend this to use persistent storage and a proper scheduler.

